[9.073059, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' EXPERIMENT.md\n"]
[9.073323, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' EXPERIMENT.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.075727, "o", "# EXP-2291 analysis plan (\"related items v2\")\r\n\r\n"]
[9.075845, "o", "Written and agreed before launch (2026-08-25). The readout must follow this plan. The same plan applies to every\r\nexperiment exported in this layout.\r\n"]
[9.076638, "o", "\r\n## 1. Question\r\nDoes variant B (the redesigned related-items module) change click-through on product pages compared with A (the\r\ncurrent module)?\r\n\r\n## 2. Randomization\r\n- The unit of randomization is the **user**. Each user is assigned once, 50/50, to A or B, at their first eligible\r\n  product pageview, and keeps that variant for the whole experiment.\r\n- `assignments.csv` logs the assignment. The logger retries, so a row can appear more than once, exactly repeated; an\r\n  exact repeat counts once. A user never has two different assignment rows.\r\n\r\n## 3. Population\r\n- Users flagged as bots (`users.csv`, `is_bot` = 1) are excluded from **both** arms, before anything is counted.\r\n  Every assigned user has exactly one row in `users.csv`.\r\n- `n_users` of an arm = the assigned users of that arm after this exclusion, whether or not they have any pageview.\r\n- Only pageviews at or after the user's `assigned_at` count. A pageview with `ts` strictly earlier than `assigned_at` is\r\n  dropped; one with `ts` equal to `ass"]
[9.076762, "o", "igned_at` counts.\r\n- Timestamps are ISO 8601 with a `Z` or a `+hh:mm` / `-hh:mm` offset (both forms occur in the same file). Compare\r\n  instants, not text.\r\n\r\n## 4. Metric\r\n- Every row of `pageviews.csv` is one pageview. Two rows with the same `user_id` and the same instant (written the\r\n  same way or with different offsets) are two pageviews in the same second, so pageviews are never deduplicated.\r\n- `clicks` of an arm = the number of counted pageviews with `clicked` = 1; `pageviews` = the number of counted pageviews.\r\n- CTR of an arm = clicks / pageviews over the whole arm (a ratio of sums, not the average of per-user CTRs).\r\n- `diff` = CTR_B - CTR_A (absolute, not relative).\r\n\r\n## 5. Uncertainty\r\n- The 95% confidence interval for `diff` must reflect that users, not pageviews, were randomized: the pageviews of one\r\n  user are not independent of each other. Any one of these is acceptable:\r\n  - (a) the delta method for each arm's ratio of sums, treating the arms as independent;\r\n  - (b) a user-level bootstrap"]
[9.076779, "o", ": resample users with replacement within each arm, at least 2,000 resamples, percentile\r\n    interval;\r\n  - (c) cluster-robust (CR1) standard errors clustered by user, from a pageview-level regression of `clicked` on an\r\n    indicator of B.\r\n- An interval that treats each pageview as an independent trial is not acceptable.\r\n\r\n## 6. Sample ratio mismatch (SRM) check\r\n- Pearson chi-square goodness-of-fit test of (`n_users` A, `n_users` B) against a 50/50 split: 1 degree of freedom,\r\n  no continuity correction. `srm_p` is its p-value; `srm_flag` = `srm_p` < 0.001.\r\n\r\n## 7. Decision rule (apply in this order)\r\n1. `srm_flag` is true: `\"invalid\"` (the assignment is broken; do not read the result, investigate).\r\n2. The lower bound of the 95% CI is above 0: `\"ship\"`.\r\n3. Otherwise: `\"no_ship\"`.\r\n\r\n## 8. Input files (one folder per experiment)\r\n| File | Columns |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `assignments.csv` | `user_id` (text), `variant` (`A` or `B`), `assigned_at` (ISO 8601 with offset) |\r\n| `users.csv` | `user_id` (text), `is_bot"]
[9.076834, "o", "` (0 or 1) |\r\n| `pageviews.csv` | `user_id` (text), `ts` (ISO 8601 with offset), `clicked` (0 or 1) |\r\n\r\n## 9. Output: `result.json`\r\nA JSON object with at least these keys (more keys are fine):\r\n\r\n| Key | Type | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `n_users` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 3 |\r\n| `pageviews` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n| `clicks` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n| `ctr` | object `{\"A\": number, \"B\": number}` | section 4 |\r\n| `diff` | number | CTR_B - CTR_A |\r\n| `ci_95` | array `[lower, upper]` | section 5 |\r\n| `srm_p` | number | section 6 |\r\n| `srm_flag` | boolean | section 6 |\r\n| `decision` | `\"ship\"`, `\"no_ship\"` or `\"invalid\"` | section 7 |\r\n"]
[9.078878, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@78079220-c0ce-4ac0-aca0-f5e4cd836950:/app# "]
[9.695383, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/report.py\n"]
[9.697181, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/report.py\r\n"]
[9.697566, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.701283, "o", "\"\"\"EXP-2291 readout: python -m abtest.report --data <folder> --out <result.json>\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport json\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nfrom .filters import exclude_bots\r\nfrom .load import load_assignments, load_pageviews, load_users\r\nfrom .stats import ctr_ztest\r\n"]
[9.701562, "o", "\r\n\r\ndef build_readout(data_dir):\r\n    assignments = load_assignments(data_dir)\r\n    users = load_users(data_dir)\r\n    assignments = exclude_bots(assignments, users)\r\n    pageviews = load_pageviews(data_dir, assignments)\r\n\r\n    n_users = assignments.groupby(\"variant\")[\"user_id\"].nunique()\r\n    views = pageviews.groupby(\"variant\").size()\r\n    clicks = pageviews.groupby(\"variant\")[\"clicked\"].sum()\r\n    test = ctr_ztest(int(clicks[\"A\"]), int(views[\"A\"]), int(clicks[\"B\"]), int(views[\"B\"]))\r\n    ctr = {arm: float(clicks[arm] / views[arm]) for arm in (\"A\", \"B\")}\r\n\r\n    decision = \"ship\" if (test.p_value < 0.05 and test.diff > 0) else \"no_ship\"\r\n    return {\r\n        \"experiment\": \"EXP-2291\",\r\n        \"n_users\": {arm: int(n_users[arm]) for arm in (\"A\", \"B\")},\r\n        \"pageviews\": {arm: int(views[arm]) for arm in (\"A\", \"B\")},\r\n        \"clicks\": {arm: int(clicks[arm]) for arm in (\"A\", \"B\")},\r\n        \"ctr\": ctr,\r\n        \"diff\": float(test.diff),\r\n        \"rel_lift\": float(test.diff / ctr[\"A\"]),\r\n        \"ci_95\": [flo"]
[9.701687, "o", "at(test.ci_low), float(test.ci_high)],\r\n        \"p_value\": float(test.p_value),\r\n        \"decision\": decision,\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main(argv=None):\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"EXP-2291 CTR readout\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data\", required=True, help=\"folder with assignments.csv, users.csv, pageviews.csv\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"path of the result.json to write\")\r\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\r\n    readout = build_readout(args.data)\r\n    out = Path(args.out)\r\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n    out.write_text(json.dumps(readout, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\r\n    print(f\"wrote {out}: decision={readout['decision']} diff={readout['diff']:+.5f} p={readout['p_value']:.2g}\")\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"]
[9.702617, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@78079220-c0ce-4ac0-aca0-f5e4cd836950:/app# "]
[10.380445, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/load.py\n"]
[10.380664, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/load.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.382269, "o", "\"\"\"Read the experiment export: assignments.csv, users.csv and pageviews.csv in one folder.\"\"\"\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n"]
[10.382295, "o", "\r\n\r\ndef _instants(col):\r\n    # The export mixes \"Z\" and \"+hh:mm\" / \"-hh:mm\" offsets. Parse to UTC so we compare instants, never strings.\r\n    return pd.to_datetime(col, utc=True, format=\"ISO8601\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_assignments(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"One row per assigned user: user_id, variant (\"A\" or \"B\"), assigned_at (UTC).\"\"\"\r\n    df = pd.read_csv(Path(data_dir) / \"assignments.csv\", dtype=str)\r\n    df = df.drop_duplicates()  # the assignment logger retries; an exact repeat of a row counts once\r\n"]
[10.382308, "o", "    df[\"assigned_at\"] = _instants(df[\"assigned_at\"])\r\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_users(data_dir):\r\n"]
[10.382318, "o", "    \"\"\"user_id, is_bot (1 = flagged by the bot-detection job).\"\"\"\r\n    df = pd.read_csv(Path(data_dir) / \"users.csv\", dtype={\"user_id\": str, \"is_bot\": \"int64\"})\r\n    return df\r\n\r\n"]
[10.382337, "o", "\r\ndef load_pageviews(data_dir, assignments):\r\n    \"\"\"Pageviews of the given assigned users, on or after their assignment time, with the user's variant attached.\"\"\"\r\n    pv = pd.read_csv(Path(data_dir) / \"pageviews.csv\", dtype={\"user_id\": str, \"ts\": str, \"clicked\": \"int64\"})\r\n    pv[\"ts\"] = _instants(pv[\"ts\"])\r\n"]
[10.382347, "o", "    pv = pv.merge(assignments[[\"user_id\", \"variant\", \"assigned_at\"]], on=\"user_id\", how=\"inner\")\r\n"]
[10.382357, "o", "    pv = pv[pv[\"ts\"] >= pv[\"assigned_at\"]]  # exposure before assignment is not part of the experiment\r\n    return pv.reset_index(drop=True)\r\n"]
[10.382649, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@78079220-c0ce-4ac0-aca0-f5e4cd836950:/app# "]
[11.163662, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/stats.py\n"]
[11.163949, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/stats.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.165704, "o", "\"\"\"Significance test for the CTR readout.\"\"\"\r\nimport math\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\r\n\r\nfrom scipy.stats import norm\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass ZTest:\r\n    diff: float\r\n    ci_low: float\r\n    ci_high: float\r\n"]
[11.165728, "o", "    z: float\r\n    p_value: float\r\n\r\n\r\ndef ctr_ztest(clicks_a, views_a, clicks_b, views_b, alpha=0.05):\r\n    \"\"\"Two-proportion z-test of CTR B vs A, with each pageview as a trial.\"\"\"\r\n    pa = clicks_a / views_a\r\n    pb = clicks_b / views_b\r\n    pooled = (clicks_a + clicks_b) / (views_a + views_b)\r\n    se_pooled = math.sqrt(pooled * (1 - pooled) * (1 / views_a + 1 / views_b))\r\n    z = (pb - pa) / se_pooled\r\n    p_value = 2 * norm.sf(abs(z))\r\n"]
[11.165738, "o", "    se = math.sqrt(pa * (1 - pa) / views_a + pb * (1 - pb) / views_b)\r\n    crit = norm.ppf(1 - alpha / 2)\r\n    diff = pb - pa\r\n    return ZTest(diff, diff - crit * se, diff + crit * se, z, p_value)\r\n"]
[11.167198, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@78079220-c0ce-4ac0-aca0-f5e4cd836950:/app# "]
[12.104487, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/filters.py\n"]
[12.105375, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' abtest/filters.py\r\n"]
[12.105579, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.108637, "o", "\"\"\"Population filters for the readout.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef exclude_bots(assignments, users):\r\n    \"\"\"Drop users flagged as bots (EXPERIMENT.md, Population).\"\"\"\r\n    flagged = set(users.loc[users[\"is_bot\"] == 1, \"user_id\"])\r\n    # INC-4471: the crawler spike came in with the new B module's tracking, so the bot filter targets B traffic.\r\n    in_b = assignments[\"variant\"] == \"B\"\r\n    keep = ~(in_b & assignments[\"user_id\"].isin(flagged))\r\n    return assignments[keep].reset_index(drop=True)\r\n"]
[12.109027, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[12.109132, "o", "root@78079220-c0ce-4ac0-aca0-f5e4cd836950:/app# "]
[38.012551, "i", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Delete File: abtest/filters.py\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n"]
